    icon: '💡',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "As a Punter, follow the standard 'Chemmy' strategy: always draw on a 5 unless your side is heavily betting against the house and you want to confuse the Banker.\n\nAs the Banker, the decision to draw is purely mathematical based on the 'Third Card Rule'. You must calculate whether drawing improves your odds of beating the *larger* of the two betting pools on the wings.\n\nBanker's Dilemma: If the Left Tableau draws a 9 and the Right Tableau draws a 2, and you have a 4, you are incentivized to draw to beat the Right Tableau, even if it risks losing further to the already-strong Left Tableau.",
    Player: "As a Punter, follow the standard 'Chemmy' strategy: always draw on a 5 unless your side is heavily betting against the house and you want to confuse the Banker.\n\nAs the Banker, the decision to draw is purely mathematical based on the 'Third Card Rule'. You must calculate whether drawing improves your odds of beating the *larger* of the two betting pools on the wings.\n\nBanker's Dilemma: If the Left Tableau draws a 9 and the Right Tableau draws a 2, and you have a 4, you are incentivized to draw to beat the Right Tableau, even if it risks losing further to the already-strong Left Tableau.",
